---
description: Do feature work on a feature branch, switching to it when it already exists
alwaysApply: true
---

# New branch required

Do not implement or commit work on `master`. Before making changes, check whether the current
branch already is the requested work.

- If it is, continue on that branch.
- Before creating or switching to a branch, check for uncommitted changes. If the worktree
  is dirty, stop and ask the user what to do; do not switch or stash. Proceed only when it is
  clean.
- If the current branch is not the requested work and that branch already exists, switch to it.
- Create a new branch from current `master` (`feat/…` or `fix/…`) only when the requested
  branch does not exist and the current branch is not that work, then make the changes there.
- Do not merge or push to `master` unless the user explicitly asks.
